content.text:
Use the `@variant` directive in your CSS, and pass it a breakpoint name such as `md`. The docs show it with `dark`, `hover` and `focus`, not with a breakpoint. Breakpoints are variants too, so `@variant md` should work the same way. I didn't find an example of it.

```css
:root {
  --my-var: 1rem;

  @variant md {
    --my-var: 2rem;
  }
}
```

- You can stack variants (`@variant md:hover`) or comma-separate them (`@variant hover, focus`).
- Source: `src/docs/adding-custom-styles.mdx`, section "Using custom CSS › Using variants" (lines 299–400).
- To define your own breakpoints, use `--breakpoint-*` theme variables. That is covered in `src/docs/responsive-design.mdx`, "Customizing your theme › Using custom breakpoints". I only read its summary, not the full section.

